  ==============================================
   KickOS 0.5.1  -  microkernel RTOS
  ==============================================
   board   rx72m
   arch    rxv3
   cpu     rxv3
   mpu     enforce
   sched   tickless

[reclaimwit] console reclaim + terminate drain witness
[reclaimwit] HOW TO READ THIS CAPTURE:
[reclaimwit]  1. this block is on the wire, so the kernel owns the console
[reclaimwit]  2. the app now publishes the console to a driver it spawns
[reclaimwit]  3. that driver never writes to a console, so the wire must go
[reclaimwit]     silent: a MUTE line below must occur ZERO times
[reclaimwit]  4. the app then SLAYS the driver and ends its task with a
[reclaimwit]     panic, whose LIVE record only the kernel writes
[reclaimwit]  5. LIVE present + MUTE absent == arch_console_reclaim fired.
[reclaimwit]     MUTE present == the publish never took, verdict void.
[reclaimwit]     both absent == the reclaim did not fire, console still dark.
[reclaimwit] drain arm: kickos_terminate follows the LIVE record, written
[reclaimwit] polled on the RECLAIMED console, so arch_console_flush_sync
[reclaimwit] alone holds the core until the shift register empties. The
[reclaimwit] record's last line must be INTACT, sentinel included.

kernel: console driver task ended, console reclaimed

=== TASK PANIC === thread 'main' ended its task
  [reclaimwit] LIVE PASS 0123456789abcdef <<<DRAIN-END>>>
